message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "OES-Resilience: Benchmarking telemetry intelligence under real-world stress"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-30"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23071166
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/oes-resilience"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  Open, reproducible benchmark for multichannel telemetry anomaly detection.
  Version 0.1.0 generates synthetic 512-channel signals under four regimes
  (stable, noisy, localized burst, global shock), scores sixteen 32-channel
  blocks with the transparent OES32 reference detector
  (0.45 max|x| + 0.35 RMS + 0.20 mean|x|, threshold 0.50), and reports
  deterministic false-positive, detection, exact-match and localization
  metrics with threshold sweeps. Synthetic data only; not quantum, not GPS,
  not a physical sensor, and no performance claims about real systems.
keywords:
  - anomaly-detection
  - benchmark
  - synthetic-data
  - telemetry
  - numpy
  - reproducibility
